From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:27:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 34/35] isolate: initialize newly selected entries in reused
 Wasm runtimes

A pooled module graph can lazily initialize an entry that was not prepared by the first invocation. Grant configuration-only initialization authority during every selected-entry preparation, not only when creating the Store. End that authority before issuing the handler capability.

Capture the new initialization reads and merge them with the retained context dependencies. Preserve earlier range hashes without rehashing unchanged dependencies; do not retain the runtime when dependency capture cannot establish reuse.

Add a cold/warm execution regression that fails with status 65 under the previous lifecycle and checks invalidation for both configuration keys. Extend the real module-graph diagnostic with an explicit preparation sequence. Update the environment test to use the current initialization transaction accessor and typed request ABI.

Validation: 28 focused initialization, capability, lifecycle and retirement tests pass, and a retained multi-entry artifact preparation sequence passes. The wider acceptance suite has three independently reproduced pre-existing failures in compound-query accounting, normalize-ID test ABI, and function-handle operation accounting.
